        "original_id": "14f4ce1b-184e-56ef-a7d6-85fab3f8dbd3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Anemopaegma, Pithecoctenium, Bignonia, Bignoniaceae\n- Mythology: Semele, Dionysus, Zeus, Cadmus, Harmonia\n- People: Diogenes of Athens\n- Works: Semele, Achilles, Helen, Herakles, Thyestes, Medea, Oedipus, Chrysippus\n\nFacts:\n- Anemopaegma is a genus of flowering plants in the family Bignoniaceae.\n- In Greek mythology, Semele was the daughter of the Boeotian hero Cadmus and Harmonia.\n- In Greek mythology, Semele was the mortal mother of Dionysus by Zeus in one of his origin myths.\n- The plant genus Pithecoctenium is closely related to Bignonia and Anemopaegma.\n- The Suda lists the works of Diogenes of Athens as Semele, Achilles, Helen, Herakles, Thyestes, Medea, Oedipus, and Chrysippus.",
